From: VLC contrib <vlc@videolan.org>
Subject: [PATCH] cryptor: require a 10.7+ deployment target for CommonCrypto

CCCryptorCreateWithMode() and CCKeyDerivationPBKDF() are only available
since Mac OS X 10.7. Gate their use on the deployment target rather than
only on the SDK version, so builds targeting 10.6 fall back to the
unsupported-crypto stubs instead of weak-linked calls that would crash
at runtime.

--- a/libarchive/archive_cryptor_private.h
+++ b/libarchive/archive_cryptor_private.h
@@ -42,7 +42,9 @@
 #ifdef __APPLE__
 # include <AvailabilityMacros.h>
 # if MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MAX_ALLOWED >= 1080
-#  define ARCHIVE_CRYPTOR_USE_Apple_CommonCrypto
+#  if !defined(MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED) || MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED >= 1070
+#   define ARCHIVE_CRYPTOR_USE_Apple_CommonCrypto
+#  endif
 # endif
 #endif

